Sval: extension JS honours the sites the user turned an extension off on

The extension hands its blocked sites to every process as it hands over
ignoreQuarantine, and holds them from its policy's creation, so no
content script runs on a blocked site during startup. The
declarativeNetRequest rules, a tab's host-permission data, activeTab
grants, tab captures, menus.onShown's page data, find, navigation events
and cookies decide access in JS without the matching
extension-blocked-sites.patch covers, and each asks the policy whether
the tab's site, or the cookie's, is blocked.

